@startuml usecase-cumulative
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica Neue"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ArrowThickness 1
skinparam UsecaseBackgroundColor #FFFFCE
skinparam UsecaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActorBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActorFontColor #000000
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #000000
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #FFFFCE
skinparam StateBorderColor #000000
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFCE
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam LifelineBorderColor #000000
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #777777

skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 110
left to right direction
title Use Case Diagram - Korean Air Reservation System (cumulative, Iteration 1-4)

' === Human actors on the LEFT (Customer is the generalized booking actor) ===
' Order Member -> Customer -> Guest so the parent Customer sits BETWEEN its two
' children: Member's generalization triangle lands on Customer's top edge and
' Guest's on the bottom edge, keeping the two hollow arrowheads clearly apart.
actor "Skypass Member" as Member
actor Customer
actor Guest
actor Administrator as Admin

' Member and Guest generalize the abstract booking actor Customer.
Member -up-|> Customer
Guest  -down-|> Customer

rectangle "Korean Air Reservation System" {

  ' Declaration order groups use cases by their owning actor so each actor's
  ' edges stay short and parallel: Member-only at the top, then the large
  ' Customer band in the middle, then Guest-only and Admin-only at the bottom.

  ' --- Skypass Member only (top band) ---
  usecase "Log in"                  as UC_Login
  usecase "Log out"                 as UC_Logout
  usecase "View my reservations"    as UC_MyRes

  ' --- Customer shared band (middle) ---
  usecase "Register Skypass membership"                 as UC_Register
  usecase "Search flights"                              as UC_Search
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Search round-trip</color>"           as UC_SearchRT
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Search multi-city itinerary</color>" as UC_SearchMC
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Search connecting itinerary</color>" as UC_SearchConn
  usecase "Make reservation"                            as UC_Book
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Book round-trip</color>"             as UC_BookRT
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Book multi-city trip</color>"        as UC_BookMC
  usecase "Enter passenger info"                        as UC_Passenger
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Select seat options</color>"         as UC_Seat
  usecase "Issue e-Ticket"                              as UC_Ticket
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Render e-Ticket</color>"            as UC_Render
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Issue linked bus ticket</color>"    as UC_BusTicket
  usecase "View booking and e-Ticket"                   as UC_ViewBooking
  usecase "Cancel reservation"                          as UC_Cancel
  usecase "Preview refund amount and policy"            as UC_RefundPreview
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Change display settings</color>"    as UC_Settings
  usecase "Pay"                                         as UC_Pay
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Pay with mileage</color>"           as UC_PayMileage
  usecase "Request refund"                              as UC_Refund
  usecase "<color:#C00000>Review refund requests</color>"     as UC_RefundReview

  ' --- Guest only (lower band) ---
  usecase "Continue as guest"       as UC_GuestEntry
  usecase "Look up reservation"     as UC_Lookup

  ' --- Administrator only (bottom band) ---
  ' Cumulative since Iteration 3 (schedule admin), so black, not red.
  usecase "Change flight status"      as UC_FlightStatus

  ' include / extend dependencies (kept local to their cluster)
  UC_SearchConn ..> UC_Search   : <<extend>>
  UC_Ticket     ..> UC_Render   : <<include>>
  UC_BusTicket  ..> UC_Ticket   : <<extend>>
}

' === Skypass Member only (top band) ===
Member --> UC_Login
Member --> UC_Logout
Member --> UC_MyRes

' === Customer (shared) associations, in declared band order ===
Customer --> UC_Register
Customer --> UC_Search
Customer --> UC_SearchRT
Customer --> UC_SearchMC
Customer --> UC_SearchConn
Customer --> UC_Book
Customer --> UC_BookRT
Customer --> UC_BookMC
Customer --> UC_Passenger
Customer --> UC_Seat
Customer --> UC_Ticket
Customer --> UC_ViewBooking
Customer --> UC_Cancel
Customer --> UC_RefundPreview
Customer --> UC_Settings
Customer --> UC_Pay
Customer --> UC_PayMileage
Customer --> UC_Refund
Customer --> UC_RefundReview

' === Guest only (lower band) ===
Guest --> UC_GuestEntry
Guest --> UC_Lookup

' === Administrator (cumulative since Iteration 3 schedule admin) ===
' Change flight status: real via FlightSchedule.changeStatus, exercised by the [ADMIN] scenario in Iter3DemoRunner.
Admin --> UC_FlightStatus

' === External systems on the RIGHT, pinned adjacent to the payment use cases ===
actor "Payment Gateway" as PG
actor "Skypass System" as SK

' Hidden ordering edges keep PG/SK to the right of the payment cluster so their
' inbound association edges stay short and do not back-run up the left gutter.
UC_Pay        -[hidden]right- PG
UC_PayMileage -[hidden]right- SK
PG            -[hidden]down-  SK

' === External-system associations (outbound calls only) ===
UC_Pay         -right-> PG
UC_Refund      -right-> PG
UC_PayMileage  -right-> SK : <<query balance>>

note as UCN
  <color:#C00000>Red use cases / flows were added in Iteration 4: round-trip / multi-city / connecting itinerary search and booking,</color>
  <color:#C00000>seat option selection, mileage payment, e-Ticket rendering, linked bus ticket, display settings, refund review.</color>
  Black use cases (authentication, one-way search and booking, passenger entry, card payment, ticketing,
  reservation lookup, cancellation, refund, admin flight-status change) accumulated across Iteration 1-3.
  'Change flight status' (real via FlightSchedule.changeStatus) is the Administrator schedule-management
  use case carried over from Iteration 3, exercised by the [ADMIN] scenario in the console demo (Iter3DemoRunner).
  'Review refund requests' (RefundReviewController approve/reject, an Iteration 4 addition) is reached from the
  customer cancellation flow (Cancellation/Refund controllers -> Navigator.showRefundReview), so it is
  associated with the Customer actor, not Administrator.
end note
@enduml
